{"parentUuid":"f0099879-9ca0-435d-bdac-edbdd9ba09b3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnvNAuaQk75y5SmBQzAa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XuYYPiy7Sqe5XDx1N52WhB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='app/scene/load.py'; t=open(p).read()\na=t.index(\"    Don't raise `min_opacity`\"); b=t.index('    \"\"\"',a)\nt=t[:a]+'''    For analysis only, such as floor maps. Never use this on a scene people will look at or that\n    views are rendered from: a few large or lone splats cover floors and walls, so removing 3% of\n    them took a test scene from 22.32 to 16.59 dB and left black holes.\n'''+t[b:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='tests/test_scene_load.py'; t=open(p).read()\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\np='docs/RESULTS.md'; t=open(p).read()\nt=re.sub(r\"\\| 2026-11-07 \\| Viktor \\| Cleaning damage.*\\n\",\"| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Cleaning damage, 40 held-out frames at 640x360 | Own splat | `clean_mask` filters, one at a time | None 22.32 dB. Size filter alone 19.81, isolation filter alone 18.02, both 16.59, with opacity above 0.05 too 16.41. Caused the black floor and door holes, in both scenes. Removing faint splats wasn't the main cause, as first thought. Viewers and renders now use uncleaned scenes | | | Roihu L40 |\\n\",t)\nt=t.rstrip('\\n')+'''\n| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Pipeline on uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply` (`lift_v3`) | 700 views, 22,671 masks | Same settings as `lift_v1` | 440 objects, 263,679 splats in them (`lift_v1`: 441, 306,360). Fewer splats, but whole pumps with clean outlines. Qwen pump labels about 7 of 12 right by eye, was about 2 of 17 | About 26 min | | Roihu L40 |\n| 2026-11-07 | Viktor | Floor map on uncleaned `Equipment Room.ply` | 700 views, our camera path clears only obstacles above 1.2 m | | Connected at 0.6 m: 11.1 m2, 42.0 m2 free. To `obj-0049` from the centre: 4.27 m, stops 0.5 m away. 384 of 440 objects reachable at 0.6 m, 210 within 0.8 m | Under 1 min | | Roihu CPU |\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat | tail -3 | cut -c1-70; K=\"$PWD/cert(13).pub\"; R=vtrilar@roihu-cpu-login1.csc.fi; B=/scratch/project_2020113/sinceai; P=\"$S/obj_v2_pkg\"; rm -rf \"$P\"; mkdir -p \"$P\"; rsync -a --timeout=120 -e \"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o CertificateFile='$K'\" $R:$B/data/scene/valmet_full/light_full.ply $R:$B/data/scene/valmet_full/light_400k.ply \"$P/\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-70; cat > \"$S/overrides_v3.json\" <<'EOF'\n{\"obj-0049\": {\"label\": \"pump\", \"mapping\": {\"asset_id\": \"ASSET-017\", \"tag\": \"P-005\", \"method\": \"manual_visual_unconfirmed\", \"confidence\": 0.3, \"note\": \"Picked by eye as the best match for a critical process pump: one of two matching inline pumps on a plinth. No tag is readable, so a person must confirm this and which of the two it is.\"}}}\nEOF\nuv run --no-sync --with numpy --with scipy python -m app.extract.finalize \"$S/lift_v3/assets.json\" \"$S/lift_v3/qwen_labels.jsonl\" \"$P/assets_final.json\" --overrides \"$S/overrides_v3.json\" 2>&1 | grep -v VIRTUAL | tail -1 | cut -c1-140; cp \"$S/lift_v3/shapes.json\" \"$S/lift_v3/splat_labels.npy\" \"$P/\"; cp \"$S/lift_v3/nav_grid.npz\" \"$P/nav_grid.npz\"; cp \"$S/floor_v2/walked.npy\" \"$P/\"; python3 - \"$P\" <<'EOF'\nimport json,sys\nP=sys.argv[1]; d=json.load(open(P+'/assets_final.json'))\nd['floor_y']=1.167; d['start']=[0,1.167,0]\nt=[a for a in d['assets'] if a.get('mapping')]; print([(a['object_id'],a['label'],a['label_grade'],a['mapping']['tag'],a['mapping']['confidence']) for a in t])\njson.dump(d,open(P+'/assets_viewer.json','w')); print(len(d['assets']))\nEOF\ntar -cf \"$S/objects_v2.tar\" -C \"$P\" . ; ls -la \"$S/objects_v2.tar\" | cut -c25-; gh release create objects-v2 \"$S/objects_v2.tar\" --target main --title \"Equipment Room objects v2\" --notes \"Private team data, delete before the repo goes public. Made from the uncleaned \\`Equipment Room.ply\\`. Run \\`make scene\\`. Objects from lift_v3 (440): assets_final.json, assets_viewer.json, shapes.json, splat_labels.npy in the original file's order. Light viewer scenes made from the original: light_full.ply, light_400k.ply. Floor map: nav_grid.npz. Camera path of our video: walked.npy. Object IDs differ from objects-v1, so re-run \\`make mapping\\`. P-005 on obj-0049 is an unconfirmed visual pick, confidence 0.3.\" 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-100","description":"Correct the record, package the new objects and publish the Release","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_read_input_tokens":397174,"output_tokens":3243,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1052},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":283,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3243,"cache_read_input_tokens":397174,"cache_creation_input_tokens":283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":283},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":15863,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XuYYPiy7Sqe5XDx1N52WhB":{"command":"cd /home/viktor-trilar/Projects/Newbies; S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-viktor-trilar-Projects-Newbies/6293938d-e68f-4310-92b7-6bf722e3d028/scratchpad; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np='app/scene/load.py'; t=open(p).read()\na=t.index(\"    Don't raise `min_opacity`\"); b=t.index('    \"\"\"',a)\nt=t[:a]+'''    For analysis only, such as floor maps. Never use this on a scene people will look at or that\n    views are rendered from: a few larg